ome in this war  that he would like to see  what does winning look like to you  but a more  victory  first of all our people would definitely  feel victory they will come back the  return of refugees is blood for the body  of ukraine without them there's nothing  the bombardments would end  we would recover our territory  there would be no russian soldiers in  our country  yes i understand they will not withdraw  from crimea and will be arguing and  negotiating for one territory or another  in the south of our country  i know exactly what has to happen after  which we can say this is victory  but if you don't mind  i'm not going to talk about it just yet  mr president we  wish you all the luck in the world  i need  half of it i think even half will be  enough  yeah it's an interview that has the  heavy feel of history just 12 hours  later you can see that interview in its  entirety now at 60minutes.com and on our  streaming service paramount plus the  entire interview with president  zielinski has also been posted on the 60  minutes youtube page check it out can we  just say that even if if by chance you  missed that interview it really is worth  your time watching i've never seen  anything like it on television the  access that scott had and i've never  seen zielinski i mean he's always a  straight talker but the way that he  talked to scott pelley and it was  interesting scott's translation yes that  he did in his own voice where you got it  was i felt we were watching something  very important in real time they're  sitting there in the dark at this hinge  moment in history and everything that  the the president is saying are echoing  back in time and also forward in the  decades
 

